{title: 351 - Thy Hand, O God Has Guided}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #351 • THORNBURY • 7.6.8.7.7.6.7.6}
{lyricist: Edward Hayes Plumptre}
{composer: Basil Harwood}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 351}
{meta: tune THORNBURY}
{meta: meter 7.6.8.7.7.6.7.6}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Thy [F#m]hand, O [D]God, [Bm]has [D]guided
[Em]Thy [A]flock [Bm]from [F#m]age to [Em]age;
[D/A]The [F#m]wondrous [Bm]tale [Em]is [Bm]written
[Em]Full [D]clear [F#m]on every [G#m]page;
[Bm]Our [F#m]fathers [G#]owned [A]Thy goodness,
[A]And we their [D]deeds [G]record;
[A]And both [D]of [A7/E]this bear [D]witness,
[A]One church, one faith, one Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Thy [F#m]heralds [D]brought [Bm]glad [D]tidings
[Em]To [A]greatest [F#m]as to [Em]least;
[D/A]They [F#m]bade [D]men rise [C#dim]and [A]hasten
[Em]To [D]share [F#m]the great King's [A]feast:
[Bm]And [F#m]this was [G#]all [A]their teaching,
[A]In every [F#m]deed [G]and [A]word,
[A]To all [D]alike [A7/E]proclaiming
[A]One church, one faith, one Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]When [F#m]shadows [D]thick [Bm]were [D]falling,
[Em]And [A]all [Bm]seemed [F#m]sunk in [Em]night,
[D/A]Thou, [F#m]Lord, [D]did send [C#dim]Thy [A]servants,
[Em]Thy [D]chosen [F#m]sons of [A]light.
[Bm]On [F#m]them and [G#]on [A]Thy people
[A]Thy plenteous [D]grace [G]was [A]poured,
[A]And this [D]was [A7/E]still their [D]message:
[A]One church, one faith, one Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]Thy [F#m]mercy [D]will [Bm]not [D]fail [A/C#]us,
[Em]Nor [A]leave [Bm]Thy [F#m]work undone;
[D/A]With [F#m]Thy [D]right hand [C#dim]to [A]help [F#m]us,
[Em]The [D]vict'ry [F#m]shall be [A]won;
[Bm]And [F#m]then by [G#]men [A]and angels
[A]Thy name shall [D]be [G]adored,
[A]And this [D]shall [A7/E]be their [D]anthem:
[A]One church, one faith, one Lord.
{end_of_verse}
